<a id="Using_a_Custom_Checkstyle_Checker_Configuration"></a>

# Custom Checkstyle Checker Configuration

You can define a custom [Checker configuration xml file](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Checker).
You can reference it through a URL, a file, or a build classpath resource.

Use the `configLocation` parameter to reference a custom Checkstyle Checker configuration.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

With this example, the plugin looks for `checkstyle.xml` in these places:

- as a file, relative to the project directory or to the directory of a parent project;
- as a URL;
- as a resource on the plugin classpath, for example in a JAR that you add as a plugin dependency, as the [multimodule example](./multi-module-config.html) shows.

Two predefined configurations ship with Checkstyle, and the plugin uses the Sun one by default:

- `sun_checks.xml`: [Sun code conventions](https://checkstyle.org/sun_style.html) (default).
- `google_checks.xml`: [Google Java Style](https://checkstyle.org/google_style.html).
